{
  "requirement": "For each project source location Habeas supplies, the address MUST consist of the project-relative file and outline selector under {cite}`requirements.references.outline_selectors`. This applies to the source metadata in mandatory inputs, acknowledgments, site matches and citation reviews, and to locations in Habeas tool diagnostics. These addresses MUST omit line and column coordinates. Quoted source retains its text, and an argument error may quote the agent's input.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover each obligation in `requirements.authoring.no_line_numbers`.\n\n**Mandatory inputs and acknowledgments.**\n- `src/authoring/mod.rs#mod[tests]/fn[subjects_of_one_kind_share_a_byte_identical_system_prompt]` builds requirement, example, citation and site subjects.\n- For each one it checks that every mandatory input and model acknowledgment carries string `file` and `item` fields.\n- It also checks that their metadata, with `text` and `body` removed, and the prompt text contain no file-with-number, line-number, `line` or `column` coordinates.\n- `src/authoring/inputs.rs#mod[tests]/fn[anchored_files_contribute_root_node_inputs]` pins the exact shape of an anchored-file input: `file`, `item`, `hash`, `kind` and `text`, with no coordinates.\n\n**Citation reviews.** `src/authoring/mod.rs#mod[tests]/fn[citation_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_the_item_and_citations]` asserts the mandatory input is `file` = `src/lib.rs` and `item` = `fn[helper]`. It also checks the prompt's item-under-review line, `<root>` for a root node, and the record's `file` and `item`.\n\n**Site matches.**\n- `src/authoring/mod.rs#mod[tests]/fn[site_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_applies_and_the_site]` checks the site subject message. It names the site as file plus selector, and the `matches` JSON carries `kind`, `query` and `item` only.\n- `src/sites.rs#mod[tests]/fn[sites_are_the_innermost_nodes_of_site_matches_and_violations_within_them]` asserts `matches_value()` is exactly `{kind, query, item, text}`.\n- Together these show the site matches are addressed by selector with no line fields.\n\n**Tool diagnostics and results.**\n- `src/authoring/line_numbers.rs#mod[tests]/fn[tool_errors_drop_the_source_line_of_a_parse_error]` covers the sanitizer. Parse-error lines, file-and-line prefixes, line/column suffixes and both addresses in a duplicate diagnostic become the file followed by `#`.\n- The same test checks that a model-supplied range in an argument error is preserved, which the text allows.\n- `src/authoring/domain_tools.rs#mod[tests]/fn[named_query_errors_identify_the_source_without_exposing_a_line_number]` checks that a named-query error contains the chapter file with `#` and no line citation.\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[source_tool_results_use_selectors_and_keep_locations_inside_quoted_code]` exercises `read_node`, `outline_source`, `search_text`, `search_structure`, a missing selector and an invalid selector end to end. It asserts selector addressing and no position fields.\n- That test also asserts that quoted source containing a file-and-line string is preserved while the surrounding metadata is clean, which covers the \"quoted source retains its text\" clause.\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[explicit_ignored_reads_return_an_error_and_the_assessment_continues]` checks that error results contain no line-number text.\n- `src/authoring/domain_tools.rs#mod[tests]/fn[domain_discovery_returns_readable_nodes_without_recording_their_contents]` and `src/github.rs#mod[tests]/fn[the_tool_reads_issues_with_the_token_and_redacts_bodies]` carry the marker, and the first also scans discovery entries for position fields.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[outline_tool_rejects_excluded_and_unreadable_sources_without_domain_reads]` and the optional-read test in `tests/authoring_cli.rs` also scan payloads for position fields.\n\nThe tests assert both the selector form and the absence of coordinates, and they preserve the allowed exceptions of quoted source and an argument error quoting the agent's input. I found no uncovered obligation and no acknowledged gap.",
  "references": "8fa50752d8f9a50e9e5440a4b718eccf25537f94f53b68d638ad560b859f823e",
